<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 27 May, from 1199 to 1967.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1199 CE <span class="tih-ago">827 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John is crowned king of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John, the youngest son of Henry II, was crowned king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. His reign saw the loss of Normandy and most of his French lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france">Philip II of France</a>, and his barons forced him to grant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-carta">Magna Carta</a> in 1215.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">John, King of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1257 CE <span class="tih-ago">769 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard of Cornwall and Sanchia of Provence are crowned at Aachen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornwall">Cornwall</a>, the second son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, and his wife Sanchia of Provence were crowned King and Queen of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen-cathedral">Aachen Cathedral</a>, the coronation church of German kings from 936 to 1531.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen-cathedral">Aachen Cathedral</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1564">1564 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">462 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Calvin dies in Geneva</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The French reformer died aged 54 in the city he had shaped into a Protestant model. His Institutes of the Christian Religion influenced Reformed churches from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1595">1595 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">431 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hugh O'Neill's Irish army ambushes the English at Clontibret</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a>, a Gaelic Irish army under Hugh O'Neill ambushed 1,750 English troops under Henry Bagenal near Clontibret on their way to relieve Monaghan Castle. The English suffered very heavy losses, their first severe setback of the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1703">1703 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">323 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peter the Great founds St Petersburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Construction began on the Peter and Paul Fortress on an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neva-river">Neva</a>, on land newly taken from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Peter made the city his capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s 'window on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1937">1937 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">89 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Golden Gate Bridge opens to pedestrians</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 200,000 people walked across the new bridge on its opening day before cars were allowed the next. Its main span was then the longest of any suspension bridge.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1941">1941 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">85 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Royal Navy sinks the battleship Bismarck</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Crippled by a torpedo hit to her rudder, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bismarck-battleship">Bismarck</a> was pounded by British battleships and sank in the Atlantic. Only about 114 of her crew of over 2,000 survived.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Australians vote to include Aboriginal people in the census</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Over 90 per cent voted to count Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people in the population and to let the Commonwealth make laws for them. It remains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>'s most successful referendum.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a></div></div></li></ol>
