<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 27 May <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ordono-i-of-asturias"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ordono-i-of-asturias.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ordoño I of Asturias</span><span class="tp">c. 821–866</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dirk-iii-count-of-holland"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Dirk III, Count of Holland</span><span class="tp">c. 981–1039</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ludovico-sforza"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ludovico-sforza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ludovico Sforza</span><span class="tp">1452–1508</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/thomas-muntzer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thomas-muntzer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Thomas Müntzer</span><span class="tp">c. 1489–1525</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-calvin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-calvin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Calvin</span><span class="tp">1509–1564</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/niccolo-paganini"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/niccolo-paganini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Niccolò Paganini</span><span class="tp">1782–1840</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jawaharlal-nehru"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jawaharlal-nehru.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jawaharlal Nehru</span><span class="tp">1889–1964</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/murray-maclehose"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/murray-maclehose.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Murray MacLehose</span><span class="tp">1917–2000</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
